\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. What service shall we render Thee
\par O Fatherland we love?
\par What gift of hand, or heart, or brain
\par May our devotion prove?
\par The coming age invokes our aid,
\par Thy voice of old inspires;
\par Shall we, Thy sons and daughters, be
\par Less worthy than our sires?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The service of the commonwealth
\par Is not in arms alone;
\par A nobler chivalry shall rise
\par Than war has ever known;
\par Glad rivalries in arts of peace,
\par True ministries of life,
\par Shall supersede the arts of war
\par And calm our feverish strife.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Too long the pagan rule of force
\par Has held the world in thrail,
\par Too long the clash of arms are drowned
\par The higher human call.
\par O comrades, seek a nobler quest!
\par O keep a worthier tryst!
\par The laws of hate have had their day;
\par Proclaim the laws of Christ!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 4. Lord of the nations, far and near,
\par Send forth Thy quickening breath,
\par Equip us for the tasks of life,
\par Save us from deeds of death:
\par Enlist us in Thy rank of fight
\par Fair freedom's holy war,
\par Whose battle-cry is Brotherhood,
\par Far-flung from shore to shore.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

